  "description": "HCOONa is Ullmanite-derived structured and crystallizes in the monoclinic C2/c space group. Na is bonded to six equivalent O atoms to form a mixture of distorted corner and edge-sharing NaO₆ pentagonal pyramids. There are a spread of Na-O bond distances ranging from 2.43-2.54 Å. C is bonded in a trigonal planar geometry to one H and two equivalent O atoms. The C-H bond length is 1.11 Å. Both C-O bond lengths are 1.27 Å. H is bonded in a single-bond geometry to one C atom. O is bonded in a 4-coordinate geometry to three equivalent Na and one C atom.",
